<section class="card" style="padding:1.5rem;margin:1.5rem 0;">
  <h2>How KillinTime works</h2>
  <p>We find the games people still love and the rights holders who own them, and we bring those games to modern phones the legitimate way: <strong>rights holders first — nothing ships without a license.</strong> The first ports are in pursuit now; when a holder says yes, that port becomes the next build, and it will be announced here and on the shelf in the console.</p>
  <p><strong>The house rules, permanent:</strong></p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Ports carry no ads. Ever.</strong> The games stay clean; the console around them carries the money doors.</li>
    <li><strong>The console itself is free.</strong> It earns from sales tolls at the website checkout, from the porting work itself, and from one honestly-labeled featured slot on the shelf.</li>
    <li><strong>The shelf is a scoreboard, not a poster wall</strong> — pursuit states are the real ones from the Codex, never dressed up.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

